    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0596" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg528"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Hale.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            23, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your despatches to No. 95,
                    inclusive. Herewith I enclose for your further information a transcript of a
                        note<anchor n="*" xml:id="d458-f1"/> which was addressed to the minister
                    resident of the United States at Quito, by the minister for foreign affairs of
                    the republic of Ecuador, on the 17th of June last, on the subject of the
                    proposition by this government to mediate by the use of its good offices for the
                    restoration of peace between Spain and the allied republics of South
                    America.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John P. Hale</hi>, Esq.,<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d458-f1" n="*" xml:id="d458-f1-content">
                <p>For inclosure see despatch No. 39, June 18th, from United States Minister to
                    Ecuador.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
